  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Fencing sphere (Footwork), Scout sphere (Calibrating Wiggle).</p>\n<p><strong>Benefits:</strong> Whenever you use the Fencing sphere Footwork talent in response to an attack made against you, you may also scout the attacker. If you successfully avoid the attack (e.g. missing or succeeding at a Reflex saving throw) and you have scouted the attacker (whether previously scouted or as part of this ability), you gain the Scout sphere Calibrating Wiggle’s bonus precision damage on your first successful attack made against the attacker before the end of your next turn, even if you do not make a charge attack against them.</p>\n<p>In addition, whenever you deal the Scout sphere Calibrating Wiggle’s bonus precision damage to a target, you may regain martial focus as a free action that can be taken even when it is not your turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Special:</strong> Abilities which function similarly to the Fencing sphere Footwork talent may be used to qualify for this feat in place of the Footwork talent (such as the Warp sphere Emergency Teleport talent, swashbuckler’s dodging panache deed, or other ability subject to GM discretion), and may treat evading an attack with such an abilities as using the Footwork talent for the purposes of this feat.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/practitioner-feats#toc110\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
